---
import { getData } from "../lib/data";
const n = getData().events.length;
---
<p class="notice">
  This database currently holds {n} cases. They are a hand-verified starting set, not a complete record of federal public corruption cases.
  Counts reflect official actions, not the total amount of corruption, and recent years are incomplete because cases are often charged years after the conduct.
  A comparison with the Justice Department's Public Integrity Section reports will be added as older cases are entered.
</p>
